<title>PORTUGAL: Portuguese maize output seen five pct up in 1996.</title>
<headline>Portuguese maize output seen five pct up in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portugal's maize production is forecast to have risen five percent year-on-year to 780,000 tonnes in 1996, the National Statistics Institute (INE) said.</p>
<p>It said that the agricultural campaign in 1996 had benefited in general from abundant spring rains which had been followed by hot weather from the second half of May.</p>
<p>The area planted to maize in 1996 was 167,000 hectares, up slightly from 162,000 the previous year.</p>
<p>--Lisbon newsroom 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
